  "comparison_method": {
    "raw_oracle": "Read bounded selected GARC members, decompress using the separately tested LZ path, then interpret signed/unsigned little-endian fields directly with Python struct. Expected cell data is the exact6400 bytes at GR section0+4; expected XYZ arrays concatenate each original16-byte collision vertex record first12bytes. Matrix field ID, camera record, all section extents, and collision group ranges are read independently from original bytes. Compare with an isolated field.c shared library through ctypes. No production parser computes expected outputs.",
    "height_oracle": "For every exact standard-walkable cell, independently intersect all exact-unique original collision triangles using XZ barycentric coordinates at local tile center(18*x+9-360,18*z+9-360). All52 produce only height0. Production first-hit queries also return0 at all52 points.",
    "test_sources": [
      "../../assets/test_field.c",
      "../../tests/test_field_viewer.py"
    ],
